1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,025
Hi there!

2
00:00:01,025 --> 00:00:04,061
In this lesson, we'll explore
your Kyntlo dashboard,

3
00:00:04,061 --> 00:00:06,805
the first screen you see
every time you log in.

4
00:00:06,805 --> 00:00:09,607
By the end, you'll know
what every number means,

5
00:00:09,607 --> 00:00:12,117
and how to use it to
make better decisions.

6
00:00:12,966 --> 00:00:13,638
Here it is.

7
00:00:13,638 --> 00:00:18,096
Think of the dashboard as your business
at a glance: your sales pipeline,

8
00:00:18,096 --> 00:00:22,798
the money in it, and how well you're
turning enquiries into paying customers,

9
00:00:22,798 --> 00:00:23,897
all on one screen.

10
00:00:24,750 --> 00:00:29,278
Most of these widgets read from Opportunities,
the deals in your sales pipelines.

11
00:00:29,278 --> 00:00:32,576
So the more carefully your team
keeps each deal up to date,

12
00:00:32,576 --> 00:00:34,532
the more you can trust this screen.

13
00:00:35,383 --> 00:00:37,052
On the left is the sidebar.

14
00:00:37,052 --> 00:00:41,625
At the top, you'll see which business
account you're in, and a search bar.

15
00:00:41,625 --> 00:00:45,890
Press Ctrl + K from anywhere to jump
straight to a contact or a page.

16
00:00:46,739 --> 00:00:48,483
Below that are your tools.

17
00:00:48,483 --> 00:00:53,110
The everyday ones sit at the top:
conversations, calendars, contacts,

18
00:00:53,110 --> 00:00:54,921
opportunities and payments.

19
00:00:54,921 --> 00:00:59,482
Further down are AI agents, marketing,
automation and your websites.

20
00:00:59,482 --> 00:01:02,030
Settings is always at the very bottom.

21
00:01:02,880 --> 00:01:06,896
At the top of the page, choose
which dashboard you're looking at,

22
00:01:06,896 --> 00:01:08,873
or click New to create your own.

23
00:01:08,873 --> 00:01:13,384
On the right, the date range controls
the period that every widget shows.

24
00:01:13,384 --> 00:01:15,114
Here, it's the last 30 days.

25
00:01:15,964 --> 00:01:17,347
Now for the widgets.

26
00:01:17,347 --> 00:01:22,949
Opportunity status counts the deals in
your pipeline, and shows where they stand.

27
00:01:22,949 --> 00:01:27,375
Here there are 16: 9 still open,
4 won, 2 lost, and 1 abandoned.

28
00:01:28,224 --> 00:01:32,030
Opportunity value turns
those deals into money.

29
00:01:32,030 --> 00:01:36,646
Each bar shows what the deals
with that status are worth.

30
00:01:36,646 --> 00:01:42,882
Open deals add up to nearly £17,000,
and the whole pipeline is worth £24,740.

31
00:01:43,734 --> 00:01:46,663
Conversion rate is the number to watch.

32
00:01:46,663 --> 00:01:50,644
It's the share of your
opportunities that you've won.

33
00:01:50,644 --> 00:01:54,550
25% means one in every four
became a paying patient.

34
00:01:54,550 --> 00:01:58,306
Underneath is the revenue
from those wins: £7,100.

35
00:01:59,155 --> 00:02:02,914
Further down, the funnel shows
how many deals reach each stage,

36
00:02:02,914 --> 00:02:06,195
and what percentage make it
from one stage to the next.

37
00:02:06,195 --> 00:02:10,312
Stage distribution shows where your
open deals are sitting right now.

38
00:02:11,162 --> 00:02:13,130
Each widget has its own filter.

39
00:02:13,130 --> 00:02:16,494
Right now they all show the
Patient Journey pipeline.

40
00:02:16,494 --> 00:02:20,049
Pick a different pipeline,
and only that widget changes,

41
00:02:20,049 --> 00:02:22,969
so you can compare two
pipelines side by side.

42
00:02:23,821 --> 00:02:28,790
And if you ever have a question about your
numbers, click Ask AI in the top corner.

43
00:02:28,790 --> 00:02:33,101
It can explain a trend, or point you
to what needs your attention today.

44
00:02:33,952 --> 00:02:35,029
Here's a pro tip.

45
00:02:35,029 --> 00:02:39,910
Make checking your conversion rate a
weekly habit, on the same day each week.

46
00:02:39,910 --> 00:02:44,917
If it drops, look first at how quickly
your team follows up with new enquiries.

47
00:02:44,917 --> 00:02:46,692
Speed is usually the reason.

48
00:02:47,542 --> 00:02:48,808
That's your dashboard!

49
00:02:48,808 --> 00:02:52,663
In the next lesson, I'll show you
how to build your own dashboards,

50
00:02:52,663 --> 00:02:55,885
with exactly the widgets each
person on your team needs.

51
00:02:55,885 --> 00:02:56,691
See you there.
